      "message": "If someone calls updateConfiguration with a non-null NetworkCapabilities, then this code will ensure that interface will not become the default. That seems reasonable: the updateConfiguration API has told us that the interface should have specific capabilities for a specific purpose, so we probably shouldn\u0027t take use that interface for tethering, because the interface will no longer be able to serve that purpose.\n\nIs your question, \"if someone calls updateConfiguration with no null capabilities, only an IpConfiguration, then what should this code do\"? If so, not sure what the answer should be.\n\nOne issue here is: if an interface is the default interface, and someone calls updateConfiguration with that interface, what should happen? I guess the code should honour the updateConfiguration command and make the interface stop being the default interface. This CL won\u0027t do that I think.",
